WEBVTT

00:13.960 --> 00:15.360
The blue ocean...

00:16.660 --> 00:18.300
The white sands...

00:19.940 --> 00:22.110
The billowing clouds!

00:23.530 --> 00:26.360
It's a perfect Okinawan beach!

00:55.490 --> 00:57.920
It shines

00:57.920 --> 01:01.980
My singing voice is endless

01:01.980 --> 01:08.560
My eternal pledge is only for you

01:08.560 --> 01:15.300
I wonder if you're your usual self

01:15.300 --> 01:20.780
I'll sparkle with you

01:20.780 --> 01:23.790
Install dream

01:28.680 --> 01:33.670
The arms of the clock advance

01:34.900 --> 01:40.090
and with them so does time

01:40.090 --> 01:47.250
When you are sad, I open my tiny arms

01:47.250 --> 01:53.600
and embrace you

01:55.610 --> 01:57.910
Fly

01:57.910 --> 02:02.200
My singing voice is tender

02:02.200 --> 02:08.580
I can remember your shape

02:08.580 --> 02:11.580
and that wasn't brought about by a program

02:11.580 --> 02:15.190
Let us experience

02:15.190 --> 02:20.880
the turmoil in my heart together

02:20.880 --> 02:23.950
Install dream

02:24.910 --> 02:29.620
Seaside Swimsuit Armor

02:24.910 --> 02:29.620
Seaside Swimsuit Armor

02:24.910 --> 02:29.620
Seaside Swimsuit Armor

02:35.180 --> 02:36.970
It's so cold!

02:36.970 --> 02:39.470
My head is stinging!

02:40.800 --> 02:42.160
I hear ya!

02:42.160 --> 02:45.510
So this is what they call brain freeze, huh?

02:47.090 --> 02:48.450
What happened?

02:48.450 --> 02:49.480
Look at this!

02:49.480 --> 02:51.100
I picked a winner!

03:16.300 --> 03:17.560
So pretty...

03:17.560 --> 03:19.260
It's so fantastic!

03:19.760 --> 03:22.520
It feels like we turned into fish!

03:29.300 --> 03:30.460
Sea slug!

03:33.040 --> 03:34.150
Stop it!

03:34.940 --> 03:36.560
It's so gross!

03:47.990 --> 03:50.000
Armor equipped!

03:50.000 --> 03:51.960
Does this look like armor to you?

03:53.530 --> 03:54.930
It suits you!

03:54.930 --> 03:57.070
What's so funny, huh?

03:57.070 --> 03:59.010
Tepid. Far too tepid.

04:01.910 --> 04:03.380
What is?

04:03.380 --> 04:05.960
I shall enjoy myself in my own way.

04:09.690 --> 04:13.390
What kinda game needs you to blindfold yourself in Swimsuit Armor?

04:13.700 --> 04:17.400
If one is to play a game upon a summer beach, there is but one option!

04:32.980 --> 04:36.800
No! Not here! Not the face!

04:36.800 --> 04:38.920
The melon's to the right! The right!

04:55.050 --> 04:56.400
Yummy!

04:56.940 --> 04:59.020
What should we play next?

04:59.400 --> 05:05.650
Hmm... isn't that Swimsuit Armor a bit lame for an Okinawan beach?

05:05.650 --> 05:08.250
You don't have anything cuter?

05:09.890 --> 05:11.790
I've no need for cuteness.

05:12.210 --> 05:15.040
This provides the greatest amount of mobility.

05:15.460 --> 05:17.510
Mobility, huh?

05:17.510 --> 05:19.540
Wanna test that theory?

05:19.850 --> 05:22.340
Interesting. I accept.

05:23.760 --> 05:25.750
Okay, here it comes!

05:46.260 --> 05:47.780
A crab?

05:50.180 --> 05:53.080
Aah! Not in my screw hole!

06:14.120 --> 06:16.930
Such is the weakness of Bikini-type Armor.

06:16.930 --> 06:18.450
Its defense is frail.

06:21.690 --> 06:23.900
M-Master?

06:28.360 --> 06:31.320
What are you all doing in your Swimsuit Armor?

06:31.320 --> 06:35.830
Oh, just doing a rehearsal for tomorrow's Okinawa trip.

06:37.270 --> 06:40.800
Practicing is fine, but I need to pack you girls up soon.

06:40.800 --> 06:42.460
We've got an early day tomorrow.

06:42.460 --> 06:44.020
Yes, Master!

06:44.740 --> 06:48.270
But I can't decide on what to wear...

06:49.370 --> 06:52.860
Master, which Swimsuit Armor do you like better?

06:52.860 --> 06:56.940
Hmm... I think this one suits you better.

06:57.720 --> 07:00.730
Oh yeah, I need to give you a coat of this before it gets late.

07:01.180 --> 07:02.490
Waterproofing oil.

07:02.490 --> 07:05.150
It also blocks UV rays.

07:06.070 --> 07:08.150
Please do, Master.

07:08.150 --> 07:10.080
Here, lie down.

07:12.170 --> 07:15.720
Your Swimsuit Armor leaves a lot exposed,

07:15.720 --> 07:17.750
so I'll need to use a lot of oil.

07:21.930 --> 07:24.240
Master, do me! Do me!

07:24.240 --> 07:26.050
Now now, wait your turn.

07:26.050 --> 07:28.230
Then I'll go next!

07:28.230 --> 07:30.550
Lene, you meanie! I'm next!

07:35.110 --> 07:36.600
Okay Master,

07:36.600 --> 07:38.280
we're going to bed.

07:39.290 --> 07:42.970
We'll be inside the bag, so take care.

07:44.330 --> 07:47.710
I've got to finish my summer homework first, and then I'll go to sleep.

07:48.480 --> 07:50.870
Don't stay up too late.

07:51.380 --> 07:53.740
Good night, Master!

07:54.760 --> 07:56.350
Yeah, good night.

08:03.550 --> 08:08.080
I'm so excited that I can't enter sleep mode.

08:09.190 --> 08:11.230
Did we forget anything?

08:14.870 --> 08:16.470
What's up, Ann?

08:18.250 --> 08:20.380
Now, for day two,

08:20.380 --> 08:23.400
I think Shuri Castle would be better than the aquarium...

08:23.950 --> 08:26.650
You should really ask Master about that.

08:26.650 --> 08:29.310
Can't we worry about that when we get there?

08:29.310 --> 08:31.190
Just go to sleep.

08:31.900 --> 08:33.790
What the heck is that?!

08:33.790 --> 08:35.900
Oh, I borrowed that from Ms. Ia. {I guess I was right to go with Ms. instead of Sis last episode.}

08:35.900 --> 08:37.830
It's Mermaid-type Armor!

08:37.830 --> 08:39.040
It's too friggin' huge!

08:39.040 --> 08:42.970
And didn't we agree on a luggage limit of 500 grams?

08:42.970 --> 08:44.520
But Ines, didn't you…

08:44.980 --> 08:46.920
Oh no, it's leaking!

08:46.920 --> 08:50.590
Why did you bring so many Jellycans?

08:50.590 --> 08:52.260
They make great snacks—

08:52.260 --> 08:55.970
I mean, they're not that heavy, right?

08:55.970 --> 08:58.300
Well that's news to me!

08:59.010 --> 09:01.250
In that case, I want to bring...

09:01.250 --> 09:03.090
What do you wanna take?

09:06.380 --> 09:08.290
No, we're not taking you.

09:14.930 --> 09:18.530
I really think Bikini-type Armor suits you best.

09:20.380 --> 09:22.040
I-I'm retiring!

09:26.330 --> 09:28.240
Let's go to sleep too.

09:28.750 --> 09:30.410
When we wake up tomorrow,

09:30.410 --> 09:32.760
we'll already be in Okinawa...

09:35.370 --> 09:36.060
Ah!

09:36.060 --> 09:37.690
What now, Lene?

09:37.690 --> 09:40.670
We should get those fried sweet buns as a souvenir!

09:40.670 --> 09:42.030
Or maybe Okinawan sweets?

09:42.030 --> 09:45.600
I <i>just</i> said to worry about that when we get there!

09:48.270 --> 09:50.960
Crap, I slept in!

09:51.440 --> 09:54.930
Wallet, handkerchief, tissues...

09:56.000 --> 09:57.700
and my passport!

09:57.700 --> 09:59.060
... dom'f need it. {Running out of the house with toast in his mouth.}

10:25.700 --> 10:27.490
We're here, girls.

10:32.020 --> 10:33.400
Come on out.

10:34.880 --> 10:37.530
Aw crap, it's the wrong case!

10:40.530 --> 10:42.780
Hello, Okinawa!

10:43.700 --> 10:44.270
Huh?

10:48.050 --> 10:50.290
Did we get...

10:50.960 --> 10:52.900
left behind?

11:03.300 --> 11:05.930
I'm sorry! I'm so sorry!

11:05.930 --> 11:08.930
You don't need to apologize so much.

11:09.230 --> 11:12.690
Master, we know you were up late with homework last night.

11:12.690 --> 11:16.180
It wasn't your fault. Yes. Yes.

11:17.040 --> 11:17.840
What?

11:17.840 --> 11:19.260
I see...

11:19.260 --> 11:22.920
So, we can't see you for three days?

11:26.150 --> 11:29.500
We'll be away from Master for three whole days?

11:29.500 --> 11:33.580
And Master was just about to enjoy himself in Okinawa...

11:34.090 --> 11:36.000
What do we do?

11:36.000 --> 11:40.420
Nothing can be done. We are unable to board airplanes.

11:44.160 --> 11:45.720
We can't give up!

11:45.720 --> 11:47.350
Huh? But...

11:47.350 --> 11:50.930
It's not like it's on the other side of the globe!

11:50.930 --> 11:52.550
We can do it somehow!

11:52.550 --> 11:54.310
We'll go by ourselves,

11:54.310 --> 11:55.610
to Okinawa!

11:58.320 --> 12:00.440
Yeah, I'm with ya, Ann!

12:00.440 --> 12:01.450
As do I!

12:02.330 --> 12:06.450
My blade would grow dull were we to remain here.{She says her skills will, but the blade is figurative here.}

12:06.800 --> 12:09.420
Let's give Master a huge surprise!

12:23.440 --> 12:25.140
Where are we now?

12:25.140 --> 12:28.340
Well, we can still see Mt. Fuji, so...

12:28.340 --> 12:30.280
Our journey is still long.

12:30.280 --> 12:34.270
Wait, we're not planning on flying the whole way there, are we?

12:34.270 --> 12:35.920
Don't worry.

12:35.920 --> 12:38.570
Let me check the transfer guides to make a route.

12:42.000 --> 12:43.950
We can ride that bus!

12:50.050 --> 12:51.990
What a nice breeze!

12:51.990 --> 12:54.080
Where is this bus headed?

12:54.080 --> 12:56.540
Guess it'd be too much to hope for a straight shot to Okinawa.

12:56.540 --> 12:59.420
We'll transfer to a train next!

13:04.660 --> 13:05.370
It is here.

13:07.330 --> 13:08.680
A freight train?

13:09.100 --> 13:10.210
Let's go!

13:22.580 --> 13:25.450
Traveling by train is nice, too!

13:25.900 --> 13:28.090
The bumpy ride feels nice.

13:28.090 --> 13:29.910
Though it makes me kinda sleepy.

13:30.210 --> 13:32.940
Good thing I packed a lunch!

13:36.600 --> 13:37.290
Ta-dah!

13:37.980 --> 13:39.870
Mountain kettle rice flavor.

13:39.870 --> 13:43.550
Wouldn't it make us even sleepier to fill up on one of those?

13:43.550 --> 13:45.810
So you don't want any, Ines?

13:45.810 --> 13:47.800
Whoah, I'll have some!

13:47.800 --> 13:50.460
We'll take turns with one sip each.

13:50.460 --> 13:52.580
I forgot to bring tea.

13:52.580 --> 13:55.240
Aw c'mon, hurry up!

13:55.240 --> 13:57.770
I brought squid flavor!

14:18.120 --> 14:19.210
Our luggage!

14:31.810 --> 14:33.080
What now?

14:34.300 --> 14:36.850
Aw, don't get depressed on us.

14:36.850 --> 14:39.180
It was our fault for dozing off.

14:39.940 --> 14:41.920
But without that...

14:41.920 --> 14:43.570
What were its contents?

14:44.500 --> 14:48.200
The spare battery packs... everyone's.

14:48.200 --> 14:49.480
Huh?!

14:49.480 --> 14:50.910
Which means...

14:50.910 --> 14:54.010
If we can't charge on the way there,

14:54.010 --> 14:57.040
we won't have the energy to make it to Okinawa?

14:57.040 --> 14:59.020
For now, let us return to the rails.

14:59.020 --> 15:01.690
We can find a Shinki Shop should we find a large town.

15:09.220 --> 15:11.050
I'm so thirsty...

15:11.560 --> 15:12.800
Here.

15:13.480 --> 15:16.060
Why'd you have to pick kettle rice flavor for this?

15:16.060 --> 15:17.910
If you can complain, do not drink.

15:22.630 --> 15:28.070
But it's strange that we've been walking so far without seeing another train.

15:28.070 --> 15:32.820
Oh yeah, there are a bunch of transfer points on railroads.

15:32.820 --> 15:36.430
Don't tell me we crossed onto an unused railroad...

15:40.610 --> 15:42.410
It seems I must tell you.

15:43.060 --> 15:47.340
It's abandoned? We must have taken a wrong turn.

15:47.340 --> 15:50.730
Where the heck are we? Pull up a map!

15:50.730 --> 15:53.000
It's no use, we're out of range.

15:53.000 --> 15:55.220
I can't connect to the net.

15:55.690 --> 15:57.850
Then we're down to our last resort. Time to fly—

15:57.850 --> 16:02.280
No. The energy consumption of flight mode is great.

16:02.280 --> 16:04.580
Entering that mode in an unknown area would...

16:07.560 --> 16:08.930
What's wrong?

16:08.930 --> 16:10.100
Something is here.

16:11.810 --> 16:12.700
A human?

16:12.700 --> 16:13.460
No.

16:13.460 --> 16:15.240
Is it a wild animal?

16:15.520 --> 16:19.240
We may be armed, but it is best to avoid combat.

16:19.870 --> 16:21.210
You're right.

16:21.210 --> 16:24.620
Fighting exhausts much more energy than just flying.

16:26.110 --> 16:29.070
Regardless, it is dark, so movement will bring danger.

16:29.070 --> 16:31.010
We shall camp the night here.

16:31.010 --> 16:33.760
We will take turns standing guard, two at a time.

16:40.970 --> 16:45.700
If we run out of power in this mountain and stop functioning,

16:45.700 --> 16:48.270
nobody will come to save us.

16:48.630 --> 16:51.680
We'll never see Master again.

16:55.640 --> 16:59.280
I wonder what Master is doing right now...

16:59.760 --> 17:01.390
Certainly asleep.

17:03.820 --> 17:06.610
This is all my fault...

17:06.610 --> 17:08.690
You are not the one at fault.

17:08.690 --> 17:11.940
But I was the one who said we should all go...

17:12.630 --> 17:16.720
Should you not have said it, someone else certainly would have.

17:16.720 --> 17:17.890
In addition...

17:19.810 --> 17:23.860
I have yet to see the ocean, so I wished to go as well, if but once.

17:23.860 --> 17:25.220
Strarf...

17:26.340 --> 17:30.310
Such thoughts may have been born from my own weakness,

17:30.310 --> 17:32.860
but I am quite skilled in survival.

17:32.860 --> 17:34.650
This situation is nothing.

17:35.780 --> 17:37.540
Thank you, Strarf.

17:39.350 --> 17:40.810
So, we are not alone!

17:56.050 --> 17:57.010
Strarf,

17:57.010 --> 17:59.300
I'll fight with you!

18:14.900 --> 18:19.660
You guys have gotta be crazy to enter the mountains in such light gear!

18:24.120 --> 18:27.190
I've got a generator, so it'll take some time,

18:27.190 --> 18:29.670
but you should all be done by morning.

18:30.140 --> 18:31.840
Thank you very much.

18:32.410 --> 18:33.730
You've saved us!

18:34.720 --> 18:39.060
But what are you doing in the mountains living in a tent all alone?

18:39.060 --> 18:41.240
Is your master not home?

18:42.830 --> 18:45.680
My master's in the SDF.

18:45.680 --> 18:46.490
Look.

18:47.440 --> 18:48.800
Over in that base.

18:50.060 --> 18:52.980
My mission is to protect this mountain.

18:53.450 --> 18:58.570
That's why I camp out here when he's on duty.

19:02.730 --> 19:04.690
South is that way.

19:04.690 --> 19:06.830
Well, I'm out.

19:06.830 --> 19:08.440
Thank you.

19:08.440 --> 19:11.580
We must surely cross swords when next we meet.

19:11.580 --> 19:14.120
Yeah, I'll look forward to that.

19:14.120 --> 19:17.590
I've always wanted to fight a Strarf model.

19:17.590 --> 19:21.060
We're truly in your debt.

19:21.060 --> 19:23.600
You even gave us spare battery packs.

19:23.930 --> 19:25.500
No problem.

19:25.500 --> 19:28.350
We're all the same when we're in trouble.

19:29.580 --> 19:31.990
Can we reach Okinawa by today?

19:31.990 --> 19:34.610
I'm sure we can make it happen!

19:35.030 --> 19:37.670
I hope you see your master safe and sound!

19:39.630 --> 19:40.780
We will!

19:47.720 --> 19:51.460
Let us go to the sea

19:51.460 --> 19:55.290
Let us travel there

19:55.290 --> 20:03.660
I can't reach it with my feet, though

20:03.660 --> 20:11.140
When I am with you, I want to go on an adventure

20:11.400 --> 20:18.370
as the southern cross shines in the sky above

20:19.690 --> 20:27.700
I won't ever forget this moment when my heart leapt with joy

20:28.200 --> 20:35.670
Let us walk into a bright and vast dawn

20:35.670 --> 20:39.450
holding boundless possibilities

20:39.450 --> 20:44.180
When I am with you

20:39.750 --> 20:39.800
